Upload the outputs of attributes found already in the store.

An attribute whose outputs are valid in the store when it is evaluated
is skipped (skipped_local) and never uploaded. The skip comes from
buildbot-nix's BuildTrigger (build_trigger.py, before the rename in
dc23225c) and assumes a closed world: an output in the local store was
either built and uploaded by an earlier CI build, or substituted from
the cache. upload.py's docstring states the assumption only
implicitly, as "each attribute's final outputs land in upload_queue".
A host that also builds outside CI (a remote builder, a developer's
build on the host) breaks it, and those outputs never reach the cache.

In a build of a push to the default branch, the skipped attributes'
outputs, all of them, now go to every uploader once the build's
attributes are scheduled, in one batch. That is the build whose
skipped outputs already get gcroots (post_process_skipped), and every
change reaching the default branch gets one, so pull request builds
and pushes to other branches stay as they were. A
buildDependenciesOnly attribute still publishes nothing. In one batch,
the uploader resolves them with one `nix path-info` call, and niks3
answers closures it already has with one request per 50 paths and
walks the closure only of the paths it lacks; that request also renews
those closures against niks3's age-based GC.

This version is unconditional, for the one host that carries it. The
version offered upstream will put it behind a host option, off by
default, with its NixOS module field, since only a host that builds
outside CI needs it.

